From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: seedds <seedds@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:55:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] packing/shader_split: read loose .nvn program files
 (Vengeance Hunters)

Vengeance Hunters keeps its eight shaders as loose *_vs.nvn / *_fs.nvn
files in the RomFS, each one NVN program behind a 16-byte header
{control length, control offset, code length, code offset}. The file
has no magic, so the generic prefilter dropped it before scan_blob
could look inside, and the split stopped with 'found no shaders in
main or the RomFS'.

scan_file_in now tries nvn_loose on every file it loads: the header's
two {length, offset} pairs must stay in the file and name a control
section and a code area of the right magic, the stage from the SPH as
usual. The programs are single-stage; '#NVN@' keys pair through the
pixel-input cover like the other single-stage sources.

Checked: build_ipa_from_nsp.py on Vengeance Hunters splits its 8
shaders (1 vertex, 7 pixel) and the packed Mac app reaches its frame
loop at 60 fps with no red line; test_split_nvn covers each stage,
non-minimal offsets and the four rejection shapes.

Found on Vengeance Hunters (01008EF020C98000), no profile yet.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#2669
Reason: Vengeance Hunters' eight shaders are loose .nvn program files (16-byte header + control section + code area) that no reader knew; the split found no shaders and the build stopped
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1309

